hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1717","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya who said: Narrated to us Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam who said: News was conveyed to us by Ibn Farrukh.

And narrated to us 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mughirah who said: Narrated to us 'Amr ibn al-Rabi' ibn Tariq who said: News was conveyed to us by 'Abdullah ibn Farrukh who said: Narrated to me Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of 'Ata', on the authority of Anas ibn Malik (RA), who said:

""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was the one who prayed the least lengthy prayer while still completing it.""

He said: ""I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and when he would give the salutation, he would stand up immediately.""

Then I prayed with Abu Bakr (RA), and when he would give the salutation, he would spring up from his place as if he were standing from hot stones.""

'Ali ibn 'Abd al-Rahman did not mention: ""He was the one who prayed the least lengthy prayer.""

Abu Bakr (RA) said: ""This is a rare narration; it was not narrated by other than 'Abdullah ibn Farrukh.""

---

**CHAPTER:**"
